IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saa-student`

-- Student Assistance Act 1973 (Cth) -- the amounts a former student owes and repays, computed from the formulas recovered on
-- 2026-10-24, beside saa-student.l4 (unchanged, where the compulsory repayment amounts still answer `not covered`).
--
-- The sidecar ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00058.formulas.md gives the formulas the text deposit lost:
--   * s 9C(1): accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt = Former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt + ABSTUDY SSL debts incurred - ABSTUDY SSL debt
--     repayments; s 9CA(2), for the financial year starting 1 July 2024: Former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt + [(ABSTUDY SSL debts
--     incurred - ABSTUDY SSL debt repayments) x 0.8];
--   * s 10F(1)(b): Applicable repayable amount - Relevant income-contingent loans liability (the compulsory ABSTUDY SSL repayment);
--   * s 12ZLC(1)(b): the same, for the compulsory Financial Supplement (FS) repayment, for 2019-20 and later income years;
--   * s 43E(6): present value = (Annual repayment / Interest) x [1 - (1 / (1 + Interest)^(Repayment period))].
-- From the text: s 9D (rounding the accumulated debt), ss 10F(1)-(3), 10G and 12ZK, 12ZLB, 12ZLC(3) (when the amount is owed, the
-- repayable debt, and "applicable repayable amount" = the least of the s 154-20(2) HESA amount, 10% of repayment income and the
-- repayable debt), s 43E(5)(b).
--
-- DEPARTURE from "borrowed terms asked as facts": s 10F(1) and s 12ZLC(1) adopt "the amount worked out under subsection 154-20(2)
-- of the Higher Education Support Act 2003". That subsection is text in the deposited HESA
-- (../../../higher-education-support-act-2003/registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.txt): "15% of the part of the person's repayment
-- income that exceeds the minimum repayment income but does not exceed $125,000" plus "17% of the part ... that exceeds
-- $125,000". It is restated here so the student can be told an amount, with the minimum repayment income and the $125,000 (both
-- indexed under HESA s 154-25) as inputs. The amounts under other Acts that make up the relevant income-contingent loans liability
-- (HESA, VET Student Loans Act, Social Security Act) are inputs.
--
-- SEAT: the student (the former student who owes the debt), as in saa-student.l4. Edition: Compilation No. 70 (C2026C00238).
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Student Assistance Act -- the debt and the repayments, computed`

§§ `ss 9C, 9CA(2), 9D -- my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt`

-- s 9C(1) "where": "ABSTUDY SSL debt repayments is the sum of all of the voluntary ABSTUDY SSL repayments (if any) paid, on or after
-- 1 July in the financial year and before 1 June in that year, in reduction of the ABSTUDY SSL debts incurred in that year";
-- "ABSTUDY SSL debts incurred is the sum of the amounts of all of the SSL debts (if any) that the person incurred during the first 6
-- months of the financial year"; the former accumulated debt is s 9B's (saa-student.l4, `What is my former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL
-- debt`). s 9D: "(1) ... disregard the number of cents"; "(2) ... less than $1.00 ... taken to be zero". (2): incurred on 1 June.
@export What is my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt, incurred on 1 June of a financial year (ss 9C, 9CA(2), 9D)?
GIVEN `my former accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt for the year (s 9B), in dollars
      `debts incurred July to December` IS A NUMBER @desc The ABSTUDY SSL debts you incurred in the first 6 months of the financial year, in dollars
      `voluntary repayments of those debts` IS A NUMBER @desc Voluntary repayments made from 1 July to before 1 June against those debts, in dollars
      `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the financial year is the one starting on 1 July 2024 (s 9CA(2))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` MEANS
    IF `before rounding` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0 ELSE FLOOR `before rounding`
    WHERE
        `before rounding` MEANS
            IF `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024`
            THEN `my former accumulated debt` PLUS ((`debts incurred July to December` MINUS `voluntary repayments of those debts`) TIMES 0.8)
            ELSE (`my former accumulated debt` PLUS `debts incurred July to December`) MINUS `voluntary repayments of those debts`

§§ `ss 10F, 10G, 12ZK, 12ZLB, 12ZLC -- how much I must repay`

-- HESA s 154-20(2), restated (see the header): 15% of repayment income above the minimum up to the upper threshold ($125,000 as
-- printed), and 17% above it.
@export What is the Higher Education Support Act s 154-20(2) amount on my repayment income?
GIVEN `my repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your HELP repayment income (or FS repayment income), in dollars
      `the minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum (HELP) repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `the upper threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The HESA s 154-20(2) amount of $125,000 as indexed for the income year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the s 154-20(2) amount` MEANS
        (0.15 TIMES `the positive part` ((min `my repayment income` `the upper threshold`) MINUS `the minimum repayment income`))
    PLUS (0.17 TIMES `the positive part` (`my repayment income` MINUS `the upper threshold`))
    WHERE
        `the positive part` MEANS GIVEN x YIELD max 0 x

DECLARE `My compulsory repayment facts` HAS
    `my repayment income`                          IS A NUMBER   -- HELP repayment income (s 10F) or repayment income (s 12ZL)
    `the minimum repayment income`                 IS A NUMBER   -- HESA, indexed
    `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold`              IS A NUMBER   -- HESA s 154-20(2), $125,000 as indexed
    `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10F(1)(b), s 12ZK(1)(b)
    `my accumulated debt on that 1 June`           IS A NUMBER
    `amounts paid or assessed against that debt`   IS A NUMBER   -- s 10G(1)(b), s 12ZLB(1)(b)
    `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10F(3), s 12ZK(2)
    `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year` IS A NUMBER  -- "relevant income-contingent loans liability"
    `the income year is 2019-20 or later`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 12ZLC(1)

@desc My applicable repayable amount: the least of the s 154-20(2) amount, 10% of my repayment income and my repayable debt
GIVEN `r` IS A `My compulsory repayment facts` @desc Your income, debt and other loan repayments for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my applicable repayable amount` MEANS
    min (min (`What is the s 154-20(2) amount` (`r`'s `my repayment income`) (`r`'s `the minimum repayment income`) (`r`'s `the s 154-20(2) upper threshold`))
             (0.1 TIMES `r`'s `my repayment income`))
        `my repayable debt`
    WHERE
        `my repayable debt` MEANS max 0 (`r`'s `my accumulated debt on that 1 June` MINUS `r`'s `amounts paid or assessed against that debt`)

-- s 10F(1): liable only where repayment income "exceeds" the minimum and there was an accumulated debt on the 1 June; (2) not if
-- the amount "is zero or less"; (3) not if the Medicare levy is nil or reduced. s 12ZK and s 12ZLC(3) the same for an FS debt;
-- s 12ZLC(1) applies to "the 2019-20 income year; or a later income year" (earlier years: not covered here).
@export How much compulsory repayment must I make on my ABSTUDY start-up loan or Financial Supplement debt this income year (ss 10F, 12ZK, 12ZLC)?
GIVEN `which` IS A `Which debt` @desc Which debt: an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt, or an accumulated Student Financial Supplement debt
      `r` IS A `My compulsory repayment facts` @desc Your income, debt and other loan repayments for the year
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much compulsory repayment must I make` MEANS
    IF `which` EQUALS `an accumulated Student Financial Supplement (FS) debt` AND NOT `r`'s `the income year is 2019-20 or later`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `r`'s `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced`
             OR `r`'s `my repayment income` AT MOST `r`'s `the minimum repayment income`
             OR NOT `r`'s `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE JUST (max 0 (`my applicable repayable amount` `r` MINUS `r`'s `my other income-contingent loan repayments for the year`))

§§ `s 43E(5), (6) -- the present value of an unpaid debt`

-- s 43E(6), formula (sidecar): (Annual repayment / Interest) x [1 - (1 / (1 + Interest)^(Repayment period))]; "interest is the
-- annual rate of interest specified by the Minister in a written notice" (an input, as a fraction); "repayment period is the number
-- of years needed to repay the unpaid amount". (5)(b): an agreement to accept part-payment needs "the agreed amount is at least the
-- present value". The statute's example: $1,200 a year, 10%, 5 years: $4,548.
@export What is the present value of my unpaid debt for a part-payment agreement (s 43E(6))?
GIVEN `annual repayment` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Secretary believes would be recovered from you in a year, in dollars
      `interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual rate the Minister has specified, as a fraction (for example 0.1)
      `repayment period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years needed to repay the unpaid amount at that annual repayment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the present value of my unpaid debt` MEANS
    (`annual repayment` DIVIDED BY `interest`) TIMES (1 MINUS (1 DIVIDED BY (EXPONENT (1 PLUS `interest`) `repayment period`)))

@export Is my offered amount at least the present value of my unpaid debt (s 43E(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the agreed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you offer to pay in full satisfaction, in dollars
      `annual repayment` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Secretary believes would be recovered from you in a year, in dollars
      `interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual rate the Minister has specified, as a fraction
      `repayment period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years needed to repay the unpaid amount
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my offer at least the present value` IF
    `the agreed amount` AT LEAST `What is the present value of my unpaid debt` `annual repayment` `interest` `repayment period`
